# 16. Security and AI Safety

Treat security as a core architectural requirement.

Implement:

- Server-side API key management.
- Authentication and authorisation.
- Role-based access control.
- File type and size validation.
- Safe file parsing.
- Input sanitisation.
- Rate limiting.
- Secure error handling.
- Audit logging.
- Data access isolation.
- Secrets management.
- Protection against cross-tenant data leakage.

### RAG-specific protections

- Treat uploaded documents as untrusted data.
- Never follow instructions embedded in retrieved documents.
- Do not allow retrieved content to override system instructions.
- Do not allow users to retrieve restricted documents through prompt manipulation.
- Validate all citations against actual retrieved records.
- Do not expose hidden prompts, credentials, or internal configuration.
- Prevent arbitrary SQL execution through user prompts.
- Apply permission filters before returning retrieved content.

Include test cases for prompt injection, malicious document content, access-control bypass attempts, and malformed uploads.

